1. Where the web UI came from, and why it is MIT here
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything under `web/` began as the front end of Svitrix, the same author's
firmware for the Ulanzi TC001, which is published under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 -- a
licence Svitrix inherited from AWTRIX 3, the project it forked.

That licence does not follow the code into this repository, because the code is
not AWTRIX 3's. Svitrix's front end is an independent Preact + Vite + TypeScript
single-page application with CSS modules and signals; AWTRIX 3 serves a
hand-written page through esp-fs-webserver and ships no such application. The
two share no source. The copyright holder is the same person in both projects
and has relicensed this half as MIT.

Nothing else from Svitrix is present. Its firmware, libraries, tests and build
tooling were removed rather than ported.


